==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Jamie Cat CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Jamie Cat is a good [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] Midranger and a decent generalist who operates similarly to [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Drunken Master Cat]] but have completely different stats and abilities. With a solid 4.6k DPS against targets at Lv.30, they function as essentially a better [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] that target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]. Jamie cat have [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] in addition to high bulk, something of a necessity for a midrange anti-Aku unit to fight against enemies like [[Condemned Peng]] or [[Fallen Bear]] despite not outranging the latter. Another ability that Jamie cat possesses is [[Strengthen]]. This increases Jamie Cat's DPS from 4.6k to 7k against Aku and substantially improve their general usage. Jamie Cat is also much more spammable than other anti-Akus, with a cooldown similar to [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] which allows him to be stacked over time.

However, Jamie Cat's Multi-Hit tends to act as a major hinderence, since Aku shields regenerate on knockback. His DPH is on the lower side, giving him bad matchups against [[Midnite D.]] and [[Ackey]], who prefer to be dealt with in one fell swoop. They also lack [[Shield Piercing]] so make sure to pair them with a [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]], so that their attacks actually land.

